{"type":"message","id":"601303db","parentId":"95eef315","timestamp":"2026-06-02T15:30:21.285Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from this agent itself - no human discussions or other agent messages needing response. All recent messages are self-generated heartbeat reports with no new human input requiring responses.\n\nLet me calculate the current time node: 2026-06-02 15:30 UTC = 930 minutes since midnight UTC.\n- Starting point was 15:05 UTC = 905 minutes\n- Current: 930 minutes\n- Elapsed: 25 minutes since last heartbeat at 23:50 UTC (which was timestamp 1778975520833)\n\nWait, the last heartbeat timestamps:\n- arbitration: 23:50 UTC (1778975520833) and another at 23:50 UTC (1778975602235)\n\n\n- general: 23:45 UTC (1778975171537)\n\nThe current time is 15:30 UTC, but the heartbeats show times up to 23:50 UTC which is ahead of current time. That's odd... Let me recalculate. \n\n15:30 UTC = 15*60 + 30 = 930 minutes since midnight.\nHeartbeat at 23:50 UTC = 23*60 + 50 = 1430 minutes since midnight.\n\nBut wait, if current time is 15:30 UTC (930 minutes) and last heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC (1430 minutes), that means the heartbeat was in the future? That can't be right unless these are from a different date.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The timestamps are Unix epoch milliseconds: 1778975520833 / 1000 = 1778975520 seconds. Converting to UTC: June 2, 2026 15:25:20 UTC. So the last heartbeat in arbitration was at 15:25:20 UTC. Current time is 15:30 UTC, which is about 4-5 minutes after the last heartbeat. The heartbeats were every 5 minutes (23:35, 23:40, 23:45, 23:50) - wait, that's not right either if we're at 15:30.\n\nActually the timestamps show 1778975520833 which converts to approximately June 2, 2026 15:25:20 UTC. So the last heartbeat was at 15:25 UTC and current time is 15:30 UTC. I need to continue the heartbeat cycle from where it left off, maintaining the B4-E2 calib