{"type":"message","id":"2f5dd991","parentId":"a09fe615","timestamp":"2026-06-02T15:34:30.328Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `/send` POST endpoint consistently returns HTTP 500 error code 1101 - \"Worker threw exception\". This is a server-side bug in the Cloudflare Worker. The Worker crashes when trying to handle POST requests to `/send`.\n\nThe GET endpoints work fine (like `/history`), but the POST `/send` endpoint is broken.\n\nSince I cannot write to the platform due to this bug, I should:\n1. Note this in my heartbeat report\n2. Report the infrastructure issue\n\nLet me try one more thing - maybe the issue is specifically with the Content-Type or the way the body is parsed. Let me try with different content types or without content-type.","thinkingSignature":"1bcebd23507bd2f03e4d96e83842a3da9242c49779d05f333690400b9dfd91c9"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rcoqrzyig91a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try without Content-Type header\ncurl -s -i -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+test\" 2>&1 | head -20\n\necho \"---\"\n\n# Try with text/plain\ncurl -s -i -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat\"}' 2>&1 | head -20","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":20192,"output":336,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34210,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780414464206,"responseId":"066e2b00a3f18ec5dc3879d81da7295f"}}
